  </div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="l-specs band-dune"><div class="wrap"><div class="row">
  <div class="it"><p class="n">2</p><p class="sub">Bedrooms</p></div>
  <div class="it"><p class="n">2</p><p class="sub">Baths</p></div>
  <div class="it"><p class="n">1,070</p><p class="sub">Sq ft<span>per tax records</span></p></div>
  <div class="it"><p class="n">2</p><p class="sub">Parking<span>assigned spaces</span></p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="sec l-unit"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="sub terra">The home</p>
  <div class="u">
    <div class="pic"><img src="/listings/331-swallowtail-ct/home-1.jpg" alt="Tall windows framing the San Bruno Mountains above the living room"></div>
    <div class="t"><p>Perched atop the prestigious Altamar at the Ridge, with the San Bruno Mountains as its dramatic backdrop, this beautifully updated top-floor corner condominium offers a serene respite from the everyday. Step inside and exhale. The open floor plan unravels effortlessly, while sweeping mountain views immediately draw the eye outward. Take a moment to breathe them in – they’re here to stay. Step outside: the private balcony, accessible from both the living room and bedroom, extends the living space into the landscape. Inspired to cook? The refreshed kitchen awaits, appointed with all-new stainless steel appliances, crisp countertops and a fresh backsplash. The adjoining dining and living areas have a versatile capability to feel intimate on a quiet evening yet expansive when welcoming family and friends.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="u flip">
    <div class="pic"><img src="/listings/331-swallowtail-ct/home-2.jpg" alt="Bedroom with a sliding door to the balcony"></div>
    <div class="t"><p>Both bedrooms are generously proportioned with functional closet space. The primary suite enjoys the privacy of an ensuite bath with double vanity, while the east-facing second bedroom glistens in the morning light. Everyday ease is thoughtfully accounted for with in-unit laundry, abundant storage, two assigned parking spaces and guest parking. Beyond your front door, an idyllic lifestyle unfolds amid scenic trails, the Mission Blue Center, Brisbane Community Pool, tennis, volleyball and pickleball courts, parks, shops and more. And when the city calls, you are well connected with convenient access to San Francisco, Highways 101 and 280, BART, Caltrain and SFO. For those seeking tranquility without surrendering the pleasures and conveniences of urban life, swoop into 331 Swallowtail and stay awhile.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec band-espresso l-comm l-story"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="top">
    <div><p class="sub">The sale</p><h2>How it <em>sold</em></h2></div>
    <div>
      <p>Bran and I put the prep budget where buyers’ eyes land first: the kitchen. New appliances, countertops and a fresh backsplash, new carpet, and a deep clean everywhere else. The bathrooms stayed simple because the comps couldn’t show us a return on anything bigger (nothing ran late, which still surprises me!).</p>
      <p>Then the price. Condos nearby were moving slowly, so we priced for the market we were actually in, with no offer date and no bidding war to manufacture. The goal was one right buyer through the door.</p>
      <p>That buyer came through the very first open house. Every dollar of prep had a reason, and the sellers could see exactly where it went.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

